{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BY26hQTB1ENTtXZrw51FYK","type":"tool_result","content":"53:The CSS reads these variables. They are shared with the other\n167:  classes: ['abc'],\n185:  <button class=\"substrate-button btn\" type=\"submit\">\n186:    <span class=\"btn-content\">Save</span>\n194:`btn` classes match what the element renders itself, and are\n233:<substrate-button id=\"labeled\" aria-label=\"Save your changes\">\n245:`popovertarget`, `popovertargetaction`, `title`, and `aria-live`.\n247:Set `aria-live` on the `<substrate-button>` host only when your app needs\n250:The host's `class` also follows onto the inner button, including a button\n251:rendered by your app before the element hydrates. Classes you add to the host\n252:are added to the inner button, and classes you remove are removed from it.\n253:The classes the element owns, `substrate-button`, `btn`, and `spinning`, are\n254:never added or removed by a host class change.\n255:On a button rendered by your app, the app owns the button's `class`. If the\n256:app changes that attribute, include any host classes it wants kept. If the\n257:app replaces its button, the new button does not receive the host class or\n263:`aria-disabled`, and native `disabled` is the source of truth.\n265:`ariaLabel` names the inner button, and the host never carries an\n266:`aria-label`. A host `aria-label` attribute moves onto the inner button,\n267:and a later `setAttribute('aria-label', ...)` also moves. The element keeps\n268:it off the host, because `aria-label` on an element with no role fails axe.\n269:Reading `el.ariaLabel` returns the inner button's label. Removing the host\n271:label, set `el.ariaLabel = null`. In Preact or another framework, pass\n272:`ariaLabel` as a property, not `aria-label` as an attribute. Removing the\n278:el.ariaLabel = 'Close the dialog'\n281:el.ariaLabel = ''\n284:`aria-live` is opt-in: set it on the `<substrate-button>` host when your app\n286:has `aria-busy=\"true\"`.\n288:Upgrade note: if your app relied on the previous default `aria-live` value,\n289:set `aria-live` on the host to restore it.\n295:starts and ends. It may use the app's visually hidden class.\n299:<p id=\"save-status\" role=\"status\" class=\"visually-hidden\"></p>\n---\n### Button attribute forwarding\n\n`FORWARDED_ATTRS` in `src/client.ts` drives both dynamic host-attribute\nmirroring and attributes supplied to the full renderer. A new forwarded\nattribute must also pass through `HANDLED_KEYS` in `src/html.ts`.\n\nAn attribute that needs its own semantics (`class`, `aria-label`) gets a\n`handleChange_<name>` method instead; any such handler suppresses generic\nforwarding in `attributeChangedCallback`. Hydration of an app-rendered\nbutton happens in the light element's `connectedCallback`.\n\nTest forwarding at the public custom-element seam with\n`esbuild test/index.ts --bundle | tapout`; cover both a rendered button and\nthe app-rendered hydration path when applicable.\n<!-- nightralph:end -->\n\n## Button tests\n---\n10:## [v0.0.54](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.53...v0.0.54)\n16:## [v0.0.53](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.52...v0.0.53) - 2026-10-15\n18:## [v0.0.52](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.51...v0.0.52) - 2026-10-03\n  \"version\": \"0.0.55\",\n    \"version\": \"npm run toc && auto-changelog -p --template keepachangelog --breaking-pattern 'BREAKING CHANGE:' && git add CHANGELOG.md README.md\",\n---\n35:export const OWNED_CLASSES = [\n46:    return (OWNED_CLASSES as readonly string[]).includes(token)\n68:    _ariaLabel:string|null = null\n168:    get ariaLabel ():string|null {\n170:        return btn ? btn.getAttribute('aria-label') : this._ariaLabel\n173:    set ariaLabel (value:string|null) {\n175:        this._ariaLabel = label\n224:     * attributes that have a specific `handleChange_*` handler. Without\n237:            typeof (this as any)[`handleChange_${name}`] === 'function'\n260:    handleChange_autofocus (_oldValue:string, newValue:string|null) {\n264:    handleChange_disabled (_old:string|null, newValue:string|null) {\n273:    handleChange_spinning (_, newValue:boolean) {\n297:    handleChange_class (oldValue:string|null, newValue:string|null) {\n317:    'handleChange_aria-label' (_old:string|null, newValue:string|null) {\n318:        if (newValue !== null) this.ariaLabel = newValue\n326:        // connected, so `handleChange_class` could not copy it then.\n328:        this.handleChange_class(null, this.getAttribute('class'))\n329:        // Likewise, a framework can set ariaLabel before that button\n331:        if (this._ariaLabel !== null) {\n332:            this.button?.setAttribute('aria-label', this._ariaLabel)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ebff6d3-1e3b-428b-bef2-f09d3ed606e4","uuid":"6c80e044-3eae-4ef5-a947-7266a21521c8","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:36:30.683Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"53:The CSS reads these variables. They are shared with the other\n167:  classes: ['abc'],\n185:  <button class=\"substrate-button btn\" type=\"submit\">\n186:    <span class=\"btn-content\">Save</span>\n194:`btn` classes match what the element renders itself, and are\n233:<substrate-button id=\"labeled\" aria-label=\"Save your changes\">\n245:`popovertarget`, `popovertargetaction`, `title`, and `aria-live`.\n247:Set `aria-live` on the `<substrate-button>` host only when your app needs\n250:The host's `class` also follows onto the inner button, including a button\n251:rendered by your app before the element hydrates. Classes you add to the host\n252:are added to the inner button, and classes you remove are removed from it.\n253:The classes the element owns, `substrate-button`, `btn`, and `spinning`, are\n254:never added or removed by a host class change.\n255:On a button rendered by your app, the app owns the button's `class`. If the\n256:app changes that attribute, include any hos