{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XL8XM4NyrhdKuyCK1E14xm","type":"tool_result","content":"## Example\n\nSee the example in [./example](./example/).\n\n```html\n<substrate-button id=\"labeled\" aria-label=\"Save your changes\">\n  Save\n</substrate-button>\n```\n\n### Attributes\n\n#### Forwarded attributes\n\nThe host forwards these attributes to its inner native `<button>` and keeps\nthem in sync when they change: `type`, `name`, `value`, `form`, `formaction`,\n`formenctype`, `formmethod`, `formnovalidate`, `formtarget`,\n`popovertarget`, `popovertargetaction`, `title`, and `aria-live`.\n\nSet `aria-live` on the `<substrate-button>` host only when your app needs\nlabel changes announced.\n\nThe host's `class` also follows onto the inner button, including a button\nrendered by your app before the element hydrates. Classes you add to the host\nare added to the inner button, and classes you remove are removed from it.\nThe classes the element owns, `substrate-button`, `btn`, and `spinning`, are\nnever added or removed by a host class change.\nOn a button rendered by your app, the app owns the button's `class`. If the\napp changes that attribute, include any host classes it wants kept. If the\napp replaces its button, the new button does not receive the host class or\nlabel again.\n\n#### Accessibility\n\nThe inner button uses native button semantics. It has no `role` or\n`aria-disabled`, and native `disabled` is the source of truth.\n\n`ariaLabel` names the inner button, and the host never carries an\n`aria-label`. A host `aria-label` attribute moves onto the inner button,\nand a later `setAttribute('aria-label', ...)` also moves. The element keeps\nit off the host, because `aria-label` on an element with no role fails axe.\nReading `el.ariaLabel` returns the inner button's label. Removing the host\nattribute later does nothing, because it is already gone. To clear the\nlabel, set `el.ariaLabel = null`. In Preact or another framework, pass\n`ariaLabel` as a property, not `aria-label` as an attribute. Removing the\nprop then clears the label.\n\n```js\nconst el = document.querySelector('substrate-button')\n\nel.ariaLabel = 'Close the dialog'\n\n// An empty string or null removes the label\nel.ariaLabel = ''\n```\n\n`aria-live` is opt-in: set it on the `<substrate-button>` host when your app\nneeds label changes announced. While the button is spinning, its inner button\nhas `aria-busy=\"true\"`.\n\nUpgrade note: if your app relied on the previous default `aria-live` value,\nset `aria-live` on the host to restore it.\n\n\n    /**\n     * The inner button's accessible name. It lives only on the inner\n     * button: `aria-label` on a host with no role fails axe. An empty\n     * string means no label, because Preact sets a removed property\n     * prop to ''. Before the element has an inner button, this returns\n     * the label it was given.\n     */\n    get ariaLabel ():string|null {\n        const btn = this.button\n        return btn ? btn.getAttribute('aria-label') : this._ariaLabel\n    }\n\n    set ariaLabel (value:string|null) {\n        const label = value || null\n        this._ariaLabel = label\n        if (label === null) {\n            this.button?.removeAttribute('aria-label')\n        } else {\n            this.button?.setAttribute('aria-label', label)\n        }\n        if (this.hasAttribute('aria-label')) {\n            this.removeAttribute('aria-label')\n        }\n    }\n\n\n    /**\n     * Apply the difference between the old and new host class lists to\n     * the inner button. Before the button exists this does nothing,\n     * because the full render() copies the host class when it builds\n     * the button.\n     */\n    handleChange_class (oldValue:string|null, newValue:string|null) {\n        const btn = this.button\n        if (!btn) return\n        const before = classTokens(oldValue)\n        const after = classTokens(newValue)\n        for (const token of before) {\n            if (after.includes(token) || isOwnedClass(token)) continue\n            btn.classList.remove(token)\n        }\n        for (const token of after) {\n            if (before.includes(token) || isOwnedClass(token)) continue\n            btn.classList.add(token)\n        }\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Move a host `aria-label` onto the inner button. The setter removes\n     * the host attribute, which calls this again with null; that call\n     * does nothing.\n     */\n    'handleChange_aria-label' (_old:string|null, newValue:string|null) {\n        if (newValue !== null) this.ariaLabel = newValue\n    }\n\n    connectedCallback () {\n        // The inner element is a native <button>, so the browser\n        // already handles Enter and Space. No keyboard handlers needed.\n        this.render()\n        // Preact sets the host class before the app's button is\n        // connected, so `handleChange_class` could not copy it then.\n        // Copy it now. Adding a token twice is a no-op.\n        this.handleChange_class(null, this.getAttribute('class'))\n        // Likewise, a framework can set ariaLabel before that button\n        // exists, so apply the stored label now.\n        if (this._ariaLabel !== null) {\n            this.button?.setAttribute('aria-label', this._ariaLabel)\n        }\n    }\n\n    render () {\n        // noop\n    }\n}\nThis file is required so that npm creates the lightningcss binary on Windows.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ebff6d3-1e3b-428b-bef2-f09d3ed606e4","uuid":"d204a7c4-cd0e-4aa3-b0df-4541578b86db","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:36:33.012Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Example\n\nSee the example in [./example](./example/).\n\n```html\n<substrate-button id=\"labeled\" aria-label=\"Save your changes\">\n  Save\n</substrate-button>\n```\n\n### Attributes\n\n#### Forwarded attributes\n\nThe host forwards these attributes to its inner native `<button>` and keeps\nthem in sync when they change: `type`, `name`, `value`, `form`, `formaction`,\n`formenctype`, `formmethod`, `formnovalidate`, `formtarget`,\n`popovertarget`, `popovertargetaction`, `title`, and `aria-live`.\n\nSet `aria-live` on the `<substrate-button>` host only when your app needs\nlabel changes announced.\n\nThe host's `class` also follows onto the inner button, including a button\nrendered by your app before the element hydrates. Classes you add to the host\nare added to the inner button, and classes you remove are removed from it.\nThe classes the element owns, `substrate-button`, `btn`, and `spinning`, are\nnever added or removed by a host class change.\nOn a button rendered by your app, the app owns the button's `class`. If the\napp changes that attribute, include any host classes it wants kept. If the\napp replaces its button, the new button does not receive the host class or\nlabel again.\n\n#### Accessibility\n\nThe inner button uses native button semantics. It has no `role` or\n`aria-disabled`, and native `disabled` is the source of truth.\n\n`ariaLabel` names the inner button, and the host never carries an\n`aria-label`. A host `aria-label` attribute moves onto the inner button,\nand a later `setAttribute('aria-label', ...)` also moves. The element keeps\nit off the host, because `aria-label` on an element with no role fails axe.\nReading `el.ariaLabel` returns the inner button's label. Removing the host\nattribute later does nothing, because it is already gone. To clear the\nlabel, set `el.ariaLabel = null`. In Preact or another framework, pass\n`ariaLabel` as a property, not `aria-label` as an attribute. Removing the\nprop then clears the label.\n\n```js\nconst el = document.querySelector('substrate-button')\n\nel.ariaLabel = 'Close the dialog'\n\n// An empty string or null removes the label\nel.ariaLabel = ''\n```\n\n`aria-live` is opt-in: set it on the `<substrate-button>` host when your app\nneeds label changes announced. While the button is spinning, its inner button\nhas `aria-busy=\"true\"`.\n\nUpgrade note: if your app relied on the previous default `aria-live` value,\nset `aria-live` on the host to restore it.\n\n\n    /**\n     * The inner button's accessible name. It lives only on the inner\n     * button: `aria-label` on a host with no role fails axe. An empty\n     * string means no label, because Preact sets a removed property\n     * prop to ''. Before the element has an inner button, this returns\n     * the label it was given.\n     */\n    get ariaLabel ():string|null {\n        const btn = this.button\n        return btn ? btn.getAttribute('aria-label') : this._ariaLabel\n    }\n\n    set ariaLabel (value:string|null) {\n        const label = value || null\n        this._ariaLabel = label\n        if (label === null) {\n            this.button?.removeAttribute('aria-label')\n        } else {\n            this.button?.setAttribute('aria-label', label)\n        }\n        if (this.hasAttribute('aria-label')) {\n            this.removeAttribute('aria-label')\n        }\n    }\n\n\n    /**\n     * Apply the difference between the old and new host class lists to\n     * the inner button. Before the button exists this does nothing,\n     * because the full render() copies the host class when it builds\n     * the button.\n     */\n    handleChange_class (oldValue:string|null, newValue:string|null) {\n        const btn = this.button\n        if (!btn) return\n        const before = classTokens(oldValue)\n        const after = classTokens(newValue)\n        for (const token of before) {\n            if (after.includes(token) || isOwnedClass(token)) continue\n            btn.classList.remove(token)\n        }\n        for (const token of after) {\n            if (before.includes(token) || isOwnedClass(token)) continue\n            btn.classList.add(token)\n        }\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Move a host `aria-label` onto the inner button. The setter removes\n     * the host attribute, which calls this again with null; that call\n     * does nothing.\n     */\n    'handleChange_aria-label' (_old:string|null, newValue:string|null) {\n        if (newValue !== null) this.ariaLabel = newValue\n    }\n\n    connectedCallback () {\n        // The inner element is a native <button>, so the browser\n        // already handles Enter and Space. No keyboard handlers needed.\n        this.render()\n        // Preact sets the host class before the app's button is\n        // connected, so `handleChange_class` could not copy it then.\n        // Copy it now. Adding a token twice is a no-op.\n        this.handleChange_class(null, this.getAttribute('class'))\n        // Likewise, a framework can set ariaLabel before that button\n        // exists, so apply the stored label now.\n        if (this._ariaLabel !== null) {\n            this.button?.setAttribute('aria-label', this._ariaLabel)\n        }\n    }\n\n    render () {\n        // noop\n    }\n}\nThis file is required so that npm creates the lightningcss binary on Windows.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XL8XM4NyrhdKuyCK1E14xm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
